      "id": "note",
      "widgetType": "markdown",
      "config": {
        "text": "# \ud83e\udde0 Query power\n\nFour live SPARQL queries, three engines \u2014 no backend, straight from your browser:\n\n- **Collection depth** (WDQS) \u2014 how many Wikidata items link to major museums' collections\n- **Women in Red** (Humaniki) \u2014 % of English Wikipedia biographies about women\n- **Most-depicted subjects** (QLever) \u2014 the top topics in Commons' structured data\n\nEdit any card's \u2699 to change the query, endpoint, or renderer.\n\nThe fourth is the **Map** renderer: a result with coordinates \u2014 a WKT `Point(lon lat)` column, or a `lat`/`lon` pair \u2014 is drawn as a map, framed to fit. It is chosen automatically when a result has coordinates, and it is in the Renderer menu when you want it anyway.",
        "refreshSeconds": 86400
      }
    },
